{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1552840-w20-m20-revised-what-happens-when-a-non-aligned-spirit-possesses-a-mortal","id":1552840,"title":"[W20/M20/Revised] What happens when a non-aligned Spirit possesses a Mortal?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-08-02T14:45:36-07:00","id":1552840,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> [W20/M20/Revised] What happens when a non-aligned Spirit possesses a Mortal?","content":"We already know about the common four types of spiritually enhanced &quot;mortals&quot; (in quotations because once fully attuned into the vessel, the fusion between spirit and mortal causes them to become one whole being and thus not mortal anymore, per se..).<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#e67e22\">Fomori </span></b>= <b><span style=\"color:#e67e22\">Bane </span></b>infested mortals, corrupted from either their direct malignant actions pre-possession or just victims of a random act of possession<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#4e5f70\">Drones </span></b>= <b><span style=\"color:#4e5f70\">Weaver </span></b>assimilated mortals from the OneSong<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#27ae60\"><b>Gorgons </b></span>= <span style=\"color:#27ae60\"><b>Wyld </b></span>taken beings whether animal, place or natural phenomenonae<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#3498db\"><b>Kami </b></span>= <span style=\"color:#3498db\"><b>Gaian </b></span>bequeathed mortals who serve in one or many ways<br /> <br /> But what about non-aligned spirits who possess mortals, who then decide to fuse with the mortal they've become attached to on a more permanent basis? Is there any precedence for this in Werewolf, and if not there, Mage?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-02T15:22:29-07:00","id":1552842,"title":"","content":"If you're using W:tA possession rules instead of having the host just be ridden temporarily, then the answer is whatever's closest to the intended metatextual effect. If the spirit is callous and cruel and is treating the host like a meat suit, they can probably be statted out as a fomor/mockery. If they're aiming for something that's long-lasting and &quot;gentler&quot; for a lack of a better term, they might use kami rules with respect to Autonomy. In general, ignore what rules say which possessed can have which powers and go by the spirit type when selecting what the spirit can get them to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-03T03:30:12-07:00","id":1552849,"title":"","content":"Part of the problem is that WtA doesn't really have the concept of &quot;non-aligned&quot; spirits. Anything that's not born of the Triat or pushed from their natural state into the service of one of them is, essentially Gaian by serving its nature without deviation from its norms. <br /> <br /> A lot of things that are spirit-adjacent but don't really follow the same rules as spirits can &quot;possess&quot; people... though that frequently results in other splats. Changelings (some types much moreso than others) are entities of the Dreaming bound to a human. Revised mummies are ghosts merged with a human (though there's a lot of variations of this in the WoD, the mummies are probably the closest in concept to WtA's possessed). Etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-03T08:04:51-07:00","id":1552853,"title":"","content":"That depends what you mean by &quot;non-aligned&quot;. In W:tA's cosmology, Umbral spirits are always aligned one way or the other. To Gaia and her Celestines and Incarnae or to the Triat (Weaver, Wyld, and Wyrm).<br /> <br /> Very few spirits could be considered non-aligned. Wraiths might be an example but, then again, although spiritual beings, in Werewolf both wraiths and spectres would be quite distinct from Umbral spirits.<br /> <br /> As a suggestion, instead of possession, non-aligned spirits (as the aforementioned ghosts) might use the <i>Domination</i> charm, described in the Possessed book, pg. 16. That's what I do in my own campaigns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28735,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28735-greywolf76","user":"Greywolf76","date":". 09-04-2025, 11:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28735-greywolf76","name":"Greywolf76","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28735_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-07T17:51:47-08:00","id":1556322,"title":"","content":"This is tricky, because WoD cosmology is split between three forces:<br /> 1 - Creation/Chaos/Creativity,<br /> 2 - Stagnation/Schedule/Consistency,<br /> 3 - Destruction/Decomposition/Corruption.<br /> <br /> Very VERY rarely do Gaian spirits have a large enough presence to assert their own force on a large enough scale to return these three back into balance (which is the plot of Werewolf in the first place).<br /> <br /> This is the tip of the iceberg, because now we have Englings, Gafflings, Jagglings, and Incarna - all who are part of a Brood (which is a &quot;spirit family&quot;) and represent some aspect of reality that we interact with or... something. <sup>I'm not a spirit expert. let me cook. lol.</sup><br /> <br /> Also, they're not going to be active in the Umbra - they're going to be in slumber first and need to be awoken via giving the spirit some Gnosis (or Quintessence if a Mage), via a process called &quot;Chiminage&quot; (which I don't fully understand but just thought to mention it).<br /> <br /> Oh, and just because a Spirit a Jaggling of an Incarna, it doesn't mean that these two are guaranteed to be part of the same spiritual faction.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Example:</b></u> A spirit of a CHURCH or religious establishment (Incarna or a powerful Jaggling) can facilitate completely different &quot;vibes&quot; (Gafflings and Englings) than the spirit of a child's cherished and loved Bible (which can gather its own essence and have a completely separate alignment).<br /> <br /> Location spirits, item spirits, road spirits...<br /> <br /> Again, <b>tip of the iceberg.</b><br /> <br /> Spirits are absolutely bonkers, and are just as much of a character as the players in their own rights.<br /> (I read on<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1481035-adapt-a-show-or-movie-s-setting-to-the-world-of-darkness/page4\"> this thread</a> that the Toons in the movie &quot;Who framed Roger Rabbit&quot; are actually very good (if comedic) representations of what spirits can be like - complete with their own perspectives and bans).<br /> <br /> I really, REALLY wish that the Axis Mundi book was still print on demand, because that book is unfortunately mandatory reading for Werewolf (and to an extent, Mage), as that book combined with Umbra: Velvet Shadow definitely help storytellers figure out how in the ever-loving flippy-flammy that they're supposed to include an entire 3/4ths of the game world into their game (that 3/4ths of the world, being <b>the Umbra</b>).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28838,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28838-dafrontlinespecter","user":"DaFrontlineSpecter","date":". 12-07-2025, 08:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28838-dafrontlinespecter","name":"DaFrontlineSpecter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-10T15:36:40-08:00","id":1556443,"title":"","content":"Well as a rule I send in an Old Priest and a Young Priest, but one must admit to being old-fashioned that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-18T18:05:40-08:00","id":1556815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greywolf76</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1552840-w20-m20-revised-what-happens-when-a-non-aligned-spirit-possesses-a-mortal?p=1552853#post1552853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That depends what you mean by &quot;non-aligned&quot;. In W:tA's cosmology, Umbral spirits are always aligned one way or the other. To Gaia and her Celestines and Incarnae or to the Triat (Weaver, Wyld, and Wyrm).<br /> <br /> Very few spirits could be considered non-aligned...</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that this is intentional. I choose to believe that the perspective of the Garou is intentionally flawed to reflect some of their weaknesses as a nation and some of the flaws in Garou religion, which, while it does have a privileged view of the universe and it's mechanics, is neither infallible nor all-knowing, and seems to me to have been influenced by centuries or millennia long war footing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27296-devidramoth","name":"Devidramoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27296_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}